#  What not to send to the Docker daemon.
#
#  These patterns are matched against the **root of the build context**, which
#  is the thing that catches everybody: a bare `node_modules/` excludes
#  `./node_modules` and nothing else, so `ui/node_modules` (161 MB) and
#  `examples/agents/minecraft/node_modules` (918 MB) were both being transferred and
#  the second was being copied into the image by `COPY examples/`. That is a
#  gigabyte of Node packages in an image with no Node in it, and about three
#  minutes of every build. `**/` is what matches at any depth.

# scratch: work dirs, engine variants, run logs, generated reports
build/
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.DS_Store
mylog.txt
**/*.log

#  Node packages, at any depth. The UI stage installs its own in the image —
#  and must, because a host's `node_modules` carries native binaries for the
#  host's platform: an esbuild built for darwin-arm64 does not run in a
#  linux/amd64 image. Copying them in would be a correctness bug and not only a
#  slow one.
**/node_modules/

#  The Minecraft demo runs from a checkout, not from the container: there is no
#  Node in the image to run it with. Its generated world and its logs are
#  regenerated on demand.
examples/agents/minecraft/world/
examples/agents/minecraft/logs/

#  vendor/ is deliberately NOT excluded: vendor/le2 is the Logical English the
#  image compiles `.le` files with, and vendor/lpsplus the two translators that
#  live in the lpsPlus repository (docs/dev/deploy.md).

#  Private notes: in the repository, not in the image, whose server publishes
#  docs/ (only the documents public_doc/1 in lps_http.pl names).
docs/vibeCodingNotes.md

#  The WebAssembly build (wasm/build.sh): a static deployment of its own
#  (docs/dev/deploy-vercel.md), not part of the image, and 26 MB of context.
wasm/dist
